update-node-alternatives (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  The maintainer scripts no longer re-register the Node.js alternatives
  on upgrade: the links live under /usr/local/bin, which Debian Policy
  9.1.2 reserves to the local administrator.

  0.4.2 changed the priority formula to major * 1000000 + minor * 1000 +
  patch. If you upgrade straight from 0.4.1 or older, apply the new
  priorities once (the manual selection, if any, is kept):

    sudo update-node-alternatives --update

  New action --install-packages [--to <version>] offers the global npm
  packages found in the other installed Node.js versions, checks their
  engines.node constraint against the target version and installs the
  selection with npm --engine-strict.

 -- Eric Lemesre <eric.lemesre@gmail.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:38:09 +0100
